        "id": "8de9f2d2"
      },
      "source": [
        "The classes are close to balanced (about 54% take the jab), so the difficulty is not imbalance but deciding **who** to post to. `employment_sector` (about half missing) and `health_insurance` (about 40% missing) are the big gaps. The next cell shows that a missing sector almost always means the person is not employed, so the gaps are kept as information instead of being filled with a guess."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "id": "fb69ffa7",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-11T11:53:24.847077Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-11T11:53:24.847012Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-11T11:53:24.858646Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-11T11:53:24.858273Z"
        },
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "fb69ffa7",
        "outputId": "4b598ef9-833d-4371-ca41-af53c5e8c43b"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "employment_sector   sector given  sector missing   All\n",
            "employment_status                                     \n",
            "Employed                    2442              25  2467\n",
            "Not in Labor Force             0            1786  1786\n",
            "Unemployed                     0             234   234\n",
            "missing                        0             269   269\n",
            "All                         2442            2314  4756\n",
            "\n",
            "missing sector belongs to someone not employed (or status missing) in 98.9% of cases\n",
            "uptake when insurance is missing: 0.462 | insured: 0.628 | uninsured: 0.258\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Is a missing employment_sector random, or does it mean something?\n",
        "sector_gap = pd.crosstab(df_train[\"employment_status\"].fillna(\"missing\"), df_train[\"employment_sector\"].isna(),\n",
        "                         margins=True).rename(columns={False: \"sector given\", True: \"sector missing\"})\n",
        "print(sector_gap)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nmissing sector belongs to someone not employed (or status missing) in \"\n",
        "      f\"{1 - sector_gap.loc['Employed', 'sector missing'] / sector_gap.loc['All', 'sector missing']:.1%} of cases\")\n",
        "print(\"uptake when insurance is missing:\", round(df_train.loc[df_train['health_insurance'].isna(), TARGET].mean(), 3),\n",
        "      \"| insured:\", round(df_train.loc[df_train['health_insurance'] == 1, TARGET].mean(), 3),\n",
        "      \"| uninsured:\", round(df_train.loc[df_train['health_insurance'] == 0, TARGET].mean(), 3))"
      ]
    },
