      "source": [
        "### B.11 Does the test set look like the training set?\n",
        "Cross-validation only predicts test performance if the two files come from the same population. **Adversarial validation**: a model is trained to tell training rows from test rows. An AUC near 0.5 means it cannot, so the files are alike; an AUC well above 0.5 would mean a shift that CV would not see."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
