      "source": [
        "## Part C. The models\n",
        "### C.1 Features and two encodings\n",
        "Two hand-made features: `precautions` (how many of the seven protective behaviours a person reports) and `doctor_and_belief` (doctor recommended it × believes the jab works).\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Encoding L (linear models and the neural network):** numeric columns get median imputation with a missing-flag and scaling; categoricals are one-hot encoded with \"missing\" as its own level.\n",
        "* **Encoding T (tree models):** categoricals are ordinal codes with missing = −1; numeric gaps stay as NaN where the model supports it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 21,
      "id": "9ee3695d",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-11T11:53:28.194961Z",
