      "source": [
        "### C.2 How every model is judged\n",
        "**10-fold stratified cross-validation, repeated twice (20 folds).** In each fold the model is trained on 90% of the residents and predicts `q` for the other 10%. Those residents are then posted to (or not) with the personal cut-off from A.3, and the fold's town bill is divided by the number of residents.\n",
        "\n",
        "The result is a mean bill per resident and its spread over 20 folds. Much of that spread comes from which residents land in each fold, so section D.2 also compares models fold by fold. AUC and Brier score are recorded too, but they do not decide anything."
      ]
    },
