        "### C.3 Comparing pre-processing options\n",
        "To see which pre-processing choices matter, each option is scored on the **same model and the same 20 folds**, so the only thing that changes is the pre-processing. Because the folds are shared, the per-fold difference from the baseline is a fair, paired comparison.\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic regression (sensitive to encoding):\n",
        "* **L-base:** encoding L as above (median + missing-flags + scaling, one-hot categoricals);\n",
        "* **L-no-flags:** most-frequent imputation everywhere, no missing-value flags (missingness thrown away);\n",
        "* **L-opinions-binned:** the three opinion scales are one-hot encoded as categories, so \"Don't know\" (3) is no longer treated as halfway between \"low\" and \"high\";\n",
        "* **L-no-engineered:** the two hand-made features are left out.\n",
        "\n",
        "LightGBM (tree model):\n",
        "* **T-native-NaN:** gaps left as NaN for LightGBM to route itself (as in C.2);\n",
        "* **T-filled:** gaps replaced by −1 before training."
      ]
    },
