      "source": [
        "### C.4 Tuning hyper-parameters\n",
        "Three model families are tuned by search. The searches optimise **log loss**: the cut-off rule only works if `q` is a trustworthy probability, and log loss rewards exactly that. Each tuned model is then judged on the town bill like every other model.\n",
        "\n",
        "* logistic regression: strength of regularisation `C` (grid search);\n",
        "* LightGBM and `HistGradientBoostingClassifier` (with native categorical splits): randomised search over tree size, learning rate and regularisation.\n",
        "\n",
        "The searches use the same training data that the cross-validation later scores, so the tuned models' CV bills are slightly optimistic (see the critical review)."
      ]
    },
