      "source": [
        "### D.2 Are the differences real? A paired comparison\n",
        "The spread above is large because some folds simply contain more older, high-risk residents than others, and that moves **every** model's bill together. Since every model was scored on exactly the same 20 folds, a fairer test is the **per-fold difference** from the leader: if a model is truly worse, it should be worse in most folds, not just on average."
      ]
    },
