      "source": [
        "### F.2 Explainability (first version, to be extended after the hackathon)\n",
        "Four techniques, from model-agnostic to model-specific:\n",
        "1. **Permutation importance in dollars, for every model:** how much the town bill rises when one column is shuffled. This is the only importance measure here that speaks the task's language (money), and it allows models to be compared side by side.\n",
        "2. **SHAP values** for the best tree model: which way, and how strongly, each feature pushes an individual's predicted chance of taking the jab.\n",
        "3. **Coefficients** of the tuned logistic regression: a transparent check on the direction of each effect.\n",
        "4. **Partial dependence** for the strongest survey answers: how the predicted uptake changes as one answer changes, averaged over everyone.\n",
        "\n",
        "All four are computed on one held-out fifth of the training data (models trained on the other four fifths)."
      ]
    },
